 "measures": [
  {
   "name": "Public Measure WD",
   "jurisdiction": "City of Decorah",
   "ballotLanguage": "\"Shall the City of Decorah, State of Iowa, issue its General Obligation Bonds or Capital Loan Notes in an amount not exceeding the amount of $20,900,000, in one or more series, for the purpose of paying costs of designing, constructing, reconstructing, enlarging, improving, equipping and furnishing municipal facilities including a new fire station and renovation of city hall, with related site improvements?\""
  },
  {
   "name": "Public Measure WE",
   "jurisdiction": "City of Spillville",
   "ballotLanguage": "Summary: To authorize a change in the use of the one percent (1%) local sales and services tax in the City of Spillville effective July 1, 2027. The use of the one percent (1%) local option sales and services tax shall be changed in the City of Spillville, effective July 1, 2027. PROPOSED USES OF THE TAX: Revenues from the local option sales and services tax (LOSST) shall be allocated as follows: Zero percent (0%) for property tax relief, One Hundred percent (100%) will be allocated annually by the City Council, for any lawful purpose, including but not limited to the following purposes: Capital equipment purchases and repairs, street, water, sewer and other capital improvement and maintenance projects, and/or for assistance to the Bily Clocks Museum and Antonin Dvorak Exhibit. The City of Spillville LOSST fund was previously established in 1991.  At that time, its use was limited to street improvements. This amendment will broaden the permissible uses of the LOSST funds, allowing for flexible planning for the use of LOSST funds, with the annual LOSST funds to be as allocated by the City Council, based on its determination of the City\u2019s changing annual needs."
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Source: 31 per-precinct/per-township official general-election sample ballot PDFs (text-extractable); found via the county site's WordPress media listing since the election page does not link them. PCT-*-DEM/REP files are June primary ballots and were excluded. Board of Supervisors elected by district; voters see only their own district: District 1 (precincts 1-2), District 2 (Decorah Twp Sup-2, Decorah Wards 1, 2, 3A), District 5 (precincts 11-12). Districts 3 and 4 are not on the 2026 ballot. County Treasurer, Recorder and Attorney candidates are printed with no party label. Township clerks with empty candidate lists are write-in only. Public Measure WD appears on Decorah ward ballots; WE on the City of Spillville ballot."
}